  "root_cause_analysis_100pct_accuracy": "AUDIT FINDING: The reported 100% cross-validation accuracy in previous versions was caused by geographic and texture collinearity shortcuts. In the processed dataset, 4 of the 6 continents (Africa, Europe, North America, South America) had invariant pH values and invariant texture values (e.g., North America clay=15.62, pH=4.9; Africa clay=23.13, pH=6.1). When latitude/longitude or raw texture fractions were used, decision trees separated continents deterministically. On LOCO cross-validation, the model encountered unseen texture ranges and coordinates, causing cross-continental generalization to drop sharply. Reporting 100% CV accuracy as true physical accuracy was misleading.",
  "shap_causality_disclaimer": "SHAP reflects model feature attribution only and does not establish physical agronomic causality."
